Abstract = {This study analyses the perception of the haptic quality of in-car push
   buttons by truck drivers. The study thus examines how a truck driver
   defines good haptic feedback with a high perceived quality by
   investigating several passenger-car push buttons which have a higher
   haptic quality than those in trucks and busses. Furthermore the study
   investigates if it is possible to translate brand-specific haptic into
   technical haptic parameters. Future research should aim to develop
   control devices that are able to transmit brand-specific quality and
   haptics to the user. (C) 2015 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V.},
