Abstract = {In the competitive employment markets of the XXIst century, one of the
   most important and influential tasks in emerging adults is to develop a
   fulfilling career, which implies identifying a calling in their career.
   Aiming to explore calling in career, this study presents the frequency
   of perceiving a calling in career, the intergroup variations on calling
   regarding age, gender and field of study and the relation between the
   perception of calling in career and living calling on a sample of 497
   Romanian undergraduate students. Implications for future research and
   practice are discussed. (C) 2015 Published by Elsevier Ltd.},
