Organization = {Web Intelligence Consortium; IEEE Computat Intelligence Soc TF BI},
Abstract = {Much knowledge has been gained about how the brain is activated oil
   audiovisual interaction. However, few data was acquired about the
   relationship between audiovisual interaction and spatial locations of
   audiovisual stimuli. Here, we investigated the mltisensory interaction
   of audiovisual stimuli presented on central and peripheral spatial
   locations. Firstly, we determined the maximal eccentricity of peripheral
   spatial location on where stimuli were presented which was 30 degrees.
   Second, the results of audiovisual interaction showed that the
   interaction of visual and auditory can have dramatic effects oil human
   perception and performance. Moreover, this effect depended on the
   spatial locations of presented audiovisual stimuli.},
