   2001},
Organization = {Western Psychol Assoc},
Abstract = {This qualitative study investigates factors that may facilitate or
   impede awareness within couples regarding the sequelae of childhood
   sexual abuse for adult females and their partner Six couples were
   interviewed about perceived effects of the abuse for self and partner
   and their perceptions regarding their awareness of these effects.
   Transcribed data were analyzed using grounded-theory methodology.
   Emergent themes regarding potential barriers to and facilitators of
   agreement are outlined in the context of the expressive and receptive
   abilities and motivations of each partner in communicating about the
   abuse. Preliminary implications for marriage and family therapy and
   further research are provided.},
