Note = {International Symposium on Memory - from Neurone to Cognition, ACAD SCI,
   PARIS, FRANCE, APR 17-18, 1997},
Abstract = {It is suggested that working memory comprises a system for the temporary
   storage and manipulation of information, forming an important link
   between perception and controlled action. Evidence is presented for,
   three-component model, comprising an attentional control system, the
   central executive, and two subsidiary slave systems. One of these the,
   the visuo-spatial sketchpad holds and manipulates spatial information,
   while the other, the phonological loop performs a similar function for
   auditory and speech-based information. Evidence is presented for the
   view that the phonological loop has evolved as a mechanism to facilitate
   the acquisition of language. ((C) Academie des sciences/Elsevier,
   Paris.)},
