   OR, OCT 07-10, 2004},
Organization = {Assoc Consumer Res},
Abstract = {This research incorporates visual triggers into traditional procedures
   of in-depth interviewing in order to elicit respondents' perceptions of
   complex phenomena with a heavy scientific background, such as
   genetically modified food. I The primary objective of the study is to
   examine the effectiveness of the use of visual triggers as research
   tools for collecting data in the domain of the unknown and to identify
   the mechanism of elicitation technique. This mechanism is found to
   include different readings of the same pictures, agreement/disagreement,
   similar readings of different pictures, voicing conscious and
   unconscious thoughts, and seeing oneself in the picture.},
