   European Agcy Safety \& Hlth Work; Lavoro},
Abstract = {This study assesses the comfort requirements on indoor environmental
   quality in hospital's ICU. It is a survey performed in Intensive Care
   Unit (ICU), in which the evaluation of the individual perception was
   performed through application of the Kano's model. It was observed that
   the air temperature according to ICU discomfort zone has a real weight
   of 0,555 in relation to environmental comfort requirements, overcoming
   the real weight of the environmental variable noise (0,337) in the same
   zone. Multinomial modeling not ratified the influence of age associated
   or not associated to the gender in the environmental comfort
   requirements in ICU.},
