   ECOLOGY},
Year = {1999},
Pages = {25-32},
Note = {7th International Congress of Ecology, FLORENCE, ITALY, JUL 19-25, 1998},
Abstract = {Managing vegetation along rivers leads to realise that there are at the
   same time good reasons to deforest and to afforest river banks. A
   comparison of different climatic zones is still needed, for example to
   account for both similarities and differences in the nitrogen retention
   capacities of riparian zones. A basic requirement is to link
   biogeochemistry and biodiversity if sustainability is the goal to
   achieve. A better understanding of the perception of riparian zones in
   human societies appears as a basic requirement to find a way between
   knowledge and management of riparian zones all over the world.},
