Note = {Workshop on Humid Buildings, GOTHENBURG, SWEDEN, AUG 28-30, 2002},
Abstract = {A cross-sectional study was carried out to investigate the occurrence of
   respiratory and other symptoms among workers in 25 buildings in
   Mauritius. Buildings were randomly selected and a self-administered
   questionnaire was distributed to the office occupants to investigate
   personal characteristics, work environment and demographic factors.
   Other questions related to the indoor climate at work included:
   perception of any health symptoms, psychosocial and physical conditions.
   A walk-through inspection of the buildings was made and some indoor
   climatic variables were measured. Some ocular and respiratory symptoms
   were related to water damage, damaged floor covering and mould growth.},
