Abstract = {The water resources management regarded as an essential tool for the
   development of Greece is discussed by the means of various factors that
   are related to the use or exploitation of water resources, such as:
   Major forces and problems, spatial distribution of water resources,
   administration structure regarding water resources management, water
   resources and regional economic development, public investments in the
   water resources sector with emphasis on land reclamation and irrigation
   - watering systems. The primary role of agriculture in both water use
   and public investment is being analysed on the basis of spatial and
   temporal-distribution for the time period 1980-2000. One of the main
   outcomes of our study was the strong variance in correlation between
   water resources use and the level of public investment.},
