   Sacramento, CA, MAY 21-25, 2017},
Organization = {Amer Soc Civil Engineers; Amer Soc Civil Engineers, Environm \& Water
   Resources Inst},
Abstract = {From 2008 to 2013, South Korea had carried out a river improvement
   project named Four River Project for flood protection and water supply
   during drought. In addition, the replacement wetlands were created in
   riverside at the same time as Four River Project to consider the
   environment of the river. However, the management problem of replacement
   wetlands has been encountered because the evaluation of the wetland
   functions for the conservation of the river environment was not done
   properly after creation of replacement wetland. So, it is necessary to
   evaluate the functions of the replacement wetlands and to establish a
   management plan of the wetlands. The wetland functions could be
   evaluated in hydrological, ecological and geological aspects. To do
   this, we compare and analyze the wetland function between replacement
   wetlands before/after Four River Project to evaluate the wetland
   function and establish a wetland management plan. Also, we evaluate the
   wetland functions associated with hydrological, biogeochemical, plant
   habitat, and animal habitat variables for the suggestion of the wetland
   management plan. Therefore, we expect that this study could be used as
   an idea for management plan of future replacement wetlands with climate
   change.},
