Abstract = {As a consequence of the rapid growth of the tourism sector, special
   emphasis is placed on destinations and tourism products connected to or
   based on certain physical and environmental factors. However, the
   negative environmental consequences of tourism are, in many cases,
   overemphasised to the social and/or economic elements of sustainable
   development. Thus, it is important to find an adequate balance of the
   elements mentioned above within tourism development in order to achieve
   an optimal way of fulfilling all requirements of sustainable
   development. In order to do this, a potential method is introduced by
   applying the Sustainability Value Map, developed originally for
   buildings and urban development projects, to the evaluation of
   sustainable tourism products. This method gives rise to further
   questions concerning the selection of the right set of indicators and
   the importance of local or regional issues. Using it as a tool, it may
   promote the process of holistic tourism planning and development.},
