Note = {4th International Conference on Environmental Science and Information
   Application Technology (ESIAT 2012), Bali, INDONESIA, DEC 01-02, 2012},
Abstract = {River pollution has been one of the main topics in the environmental
   issue of urban Dhaka, the capital city of Bangladesh. However, this
   study was conducted to find out the pollution situation of the river and
   the health problem of the residents of area. The results of the sampling
   programme clearly determine that the water quality of Turag River may
   not be in a position to sustain the aquatic life as well as not suitable
   for using for domestic purpose. This is indicated by the very low DO
   levels as well other measured parameters in the river, as has been shown
   by the analysis of samples collected for the study and by the available
   data. The maximum recorded value of color is 625 ptcu, turbidity is
   97.2, BOD5 is 4.65 mg/l, hardness is1816 mg/l, Cl is 5 mg/I, CO2 is
   15.5, and COD is 78 mg/l respectively. The maximum concentration of BOD,
   COD, Turbidity, Alkalinity, Hardness and Total Dissolved Solids found in
   the Turag river is much higher than the standard permissible limit. On
   the other hand, the study provides evidence that local communities are
   suffering from a variety of health problems included skin, diarrhea,
   dysentery, respiratory illnesses, anemia and complications in
   childbirth. The people lives in the area are also suffering by the odor
   pollution and by the respiratory problems.},
