   Construct \& Building Phys; Tech Chamber Greece},
Abstract = {The total number of buildings in Greece amount to 4.1 million of which
   20\% are exclusive non-residential buildings that usually have high
   energy consumption due to specific building uses. The present work
   exploits data from energy performance certificates to derive relevant
   benchmarks. Recommended energy conservation measures are identified and
   analysed to identify the most common measures. Finally, a methodology is
   elaborated for deriving empirical adaptation factors to relate the
   normative calculated heating energy consumption with actual energy use,
   if available. (C) 2017 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V.},
