   \& Hlth; Int Council Res \& Innovat Bldg \& Construct; European Commiss
   Asia Pro Eco Programme Promot Sustainable Solut Environm Europe \& Asia;
   Korean Soc Indoor Environm; Soc Indoor Environm},
Abstract = {This study explores the correlation of upper extremity skin temperature
   with overall body thermal sensation. Time-series temperature
   measurements on finger, hand, and forearm were taken during a program of
   tests in which subjects were heated and cooled. Subjective perception of
   whole body thermal sensation and comfort was collected with nine-point
   analog scales. The findings suggest that one can use finger temperature,
   or the temperature gradient from finger to forearm, to predict whether a
   subject is feeling cold or warm, or is currently neutral but in the
   process of becoming cold. The findings may be used to develop novel ways
   to monitor thermal sensation in indoor environments.},
