   PROTECTION},
Year = {1997},
Pages = {157-163},
Note = {International Oil Spill Conference - Improving Environmental Protection,
   FT LAUDERDALE, FL, APR 07-10, 1997},
Organization = {US Coast Guard; US EPA; Amer Petr Inst; Int Petr Ind Environm Conservat
   Assoc; Int Maritime Org},
Abstract = {It is commonly accepted that oil spills are unintended, unanticipated
   events due primarily to equipment failure or human error. Public
   perception generally attributes oils spills to accidents like groundings
   of transport vessels or ruptures of pipelines and tanks. Unfortunately,
   in reality there are a number of intended, anticipated events that
   result in oil spills that are equally,: if not more, devastating to the
   environment. Most prominent among these events are war, terrorism,
   vandalism, and theft. This paper seeks to examine some of the oil spills
   caused by human intent, their impact on the environment, and holy
   prevention and response planning can mitigate some of their
   consequences.},
