   Sci \& Arts; Georgian Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {Digital game culture belongs to the most important phenomena of the last
   decades. Special attention has been aroused by Role-Playing-Games
   (RPGs). In the course of time there has been formed a rather extensive
   subculture under their influence. RPGs offer a unique experience of
   existence in a different reality in the made-up virtual world, where a
   human gains a new identity, new possibilities to live{''}. In the paper
   we deal with mapping and typology of characters in RPGs and their
   connection to archetype roles. Crucial is the perception of projection
   as a psychic ability to project own psychic contents into exterior
   objects or fantasy.},
