   and Annual Symposium of Science and Technology Association, Wuhan,
   PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT, 2010},
Abstract = {The study employs a survey method for identifying factors to take
   environmental responsibility within Small and medium enterprises (SMEs)
   in the Yangtze River Delta We uncover SMEs' views on motivations, the
   drivers and barriers to take corporate environmental responsibility
   (CER) and general perceptions on related issues Results show that the
   dominant driver for CER is government legislative policies,
   incentive-Based policies play an important role m the behavior of CER It
   is found that the major barriers to the implementation of CER are the
   cost of implementing environmental practices The survey also suggested
   that SMEs can gain a competitive advantage and create sustainable
   business by adopting environmental good practices},
