Title = {Use of bioindicators as early warning system for air pollution due to
   automobile exhaust pollutants},
Booktitle = {Proceedings of the World Engineers' Convention 2004: Vol D, Environment
   Protection and Disaster Mitigation},
Year = {2004},
Pages = {83-90},
Note = {World Engineers Convention 2004, Shanghai, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 02-06,
   2004},
Organization = {Shanghai Baosteel Grp Corp; Shanghai Automot Ind Corp; China Natl
   Petroleum Corp; China Petrochem Corp; State Grid Corp China; Shanghai
   Huizhong Automat Mfg Co Ltd; China Aerosp Sci \& Technol Corp; China
   Yangtze Three Gorges Project Dev Corp; China Natl Nucl Corp; BMW Grp
   Beijing; Chun Wo Construct \& Engn Co Ltd; Shui On Land Ltd; Air China},
Abstract = {Today's growing population and increasing urbanization has resulted in
   sudden increase in number of vehicles. The problem posed with vehicles
   is due to discharge of pollutants ( CO, HCl, Pb, SOx, NOx, PM. etc.). It
   is known fact that 60 \% of air pollution in city is caused by
   automobiles only 1. The effect of these pollutants is observed at acute
   level on sensitive species both plants and animals. Plants are
   considered for investigation of effect of autoexhaust pollutants.
   Response of plants towards air can be assessed by air pollution
   tolerance index. Acute \& chronic symptoms can be utilized to
   investigate accumulation of pollutants. Plants are affected by increased
   localized atmospheric pollution. But some plant species and varieties
   are so sensitive that they can be conveniently employed as biological
   indicators or monitors for specific pollutants. They can further assist
   human in planning the urban cities. Plants are stationary so they show
   the localized effect of pollution. A relationship can be derived within
   the Bioindicators and vehicular pollution load. This relationship can be
   utilized to plan the vehicular pollution load along a specific pathway.
   To support the study a case has been considered.},
