   Chinese Leadership Styles},
Booktitle = {CONFERENCE ON PSYCHOLOGY AND SOCIAL HARMONY (CPSH2011)},
Year = {2011},
Pages = {61+},
Note = {Conference on Psychology and Social Harmony (CPSH 2011), Wuhan, PEOPLES
   R CHINA, APR 08-10, 2011},
Organization = {Wuhan Univ; Huazhong Normal Univ; Huazhong Univ Sci \& Technol; Jinan
   Univ; James Madison Univ; Sci Res Publish; Engn Informat Inst; Chongqing
   VIP Informat Co, Ltd},
Abstract = {On the basis of theoretical considerations about possible leadership
   styles in China, we developed a questionnaire for measuring the
   perception of leadership styles by Chinese employees. The questionnaire
   was tested by a sample of 201 participants working in different cities
   of China as Shanghai, Beijing, Fuzhou, Nanjing and some others. As a
   result, some items were omitted or modified. The questionnaire was
   formulated in Mandarin. Further analysis revealed the measuring of
   genuine Chinese Leadership Styles. A resulting comparative analysis with
   data from Germany revealed that the Questionnaire is able to measure the
   genuine Chinese Leadership Styles and differentiate them from those
   outside of China.},
