   Tourism Chamber Commerce; Lingnan Int Grp; Chime Long Grp; Hengda Hotel
   Management Grp; Amer Scholar Press; Jinan Univ, Alumni Assoc},
Abstract = {Shopping is a pervasive and an essential tourism activity. In recent
   years, the discussion of perceived tourism shopping quality has obtained
   substantial attention. But so far, there are no specialized researches
   on studying the dimensions and contents of tourists' perceived shopping
   quality. The unit of this study is Mainland Chinese tourist shopping in
   Hong Kong; 100 valid questionnaires were collected and used for data
   analysis. The results indicate that tourists usually evaluate their
   shopping quality perception from four aspects including product, price,
   environment and service. Moreover, tourists' perceived shopping quality
   has a positive impact on tourism shopping satisfaction, while tourism
   shopping satisfaction has a negative impact on behavioral intentions.},
