Note = {8th World STI/AIDS Congress, Punta del Este, URUGUAY, DEC 02-05, 2003},
Abstract = {A community action plan was developed and implemented to reduce
   disparities in HIV disease among African-American, Hispanic-American,
   Haitian and other Caribbean populations of African ancestry in Broward
   County, Florida. Computer-assisted telephone interview Surveys with
   residents 18 to 39 years of age were conducted as the program was being
   introduced in 2001 and one year later. Perception of the local HIV/AIDS
   problem, awareness of the REACH 2010 project, and participation in AIDS
   advocacy and prevention activities among community residents increased.
   Short-term impact of interventions on target populations was observed,
   but considerably more progress will be required to stimulate
   participation in community-wide HIV and STI prevention efforts.},
