   dissatisfaction with the quality of carp. Patients complain that
   providers fail to appreciate the impact of symploms on junction and
   neglect discussion of diagnosis and prognosis. Physician-patient
   communication appears to be central to patients' perceptions of quality
   of care. Specifically, addressing patients' expectations may influence
   satisfaction as much, or more than, the outcome of treatment itse (. The
