   MATHEMATICAL BIOLOGY AND ECOLOGY},
Series = {Mathematics and Computers in Science and Engineering},
Year = {2008},
Pages = {18-23},
Note = {4th WSEAS International Conference on Mathematical Biology and Ecology,
   Acapulco, MEXICO, JAN 25-27, 2008},
Abstract = {A mathematical model of visceral perception was constructed, comprising
   primary sensory, motor, intestinofugal and principal neurons,
   interstitial cells of Cajal and smooth muscle elements that are arranged
   in a functional circuit through chemical synapses. The mathematical
   description of constructive elements was based on detailed
   morphological, anatomical, electro-physiological and
   neuropharmacological characteristics of cells and chemical processes of
   electrochemical coupling. Emphasis was given to signal transduction
   mechanisms that involved multiple neurotransmitters and receptor
   polymodality. Results of computer simulations reproduced patterns of
   electrical activity of neurons and mechanical responses of the smooth
   muscle similar to those observed experimentally and provide
   neurochemical bases for explanation of pathophysiological mechanisms of
   visceral nociception.},
