   17-21, 2003},
Organization = {IEEE Engn Med \& Biol Soc; Coral; Univ Autonome Metropolitana; Sandia
   Natl Lab},
Abstract = {This paper describes the design of an instrument for the functional and
   objective evaluation of the visual field, as well as an ophthalmologic
   methodology based on a Video-Oculography system (VOG). This objective
   evaluation methodology is carried out using the visual evoked potentials
   (VEP) and the pupillary response (PR).
   The system sustains its objectivity in the digital processing of the PR
   recorded by the VOG system during the test caused by the photomotor
   reflex, and in the analysis of the VEP.
   The analysis of the PR digitalized and the VEP recorded, give us an idea
   of the visual condition of the observer, without involve the dependence
   of their perception.},
